<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 18 March, from 1068 to 2014.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/arabia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arabia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1068">1068 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">958 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A major earthquake strikes Arabia and the Levant</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first of two major Near Eastern earthquakes that year had its epicentre in the northwestern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-peninsula">Arabian Peninsula</a>, around Tabuk. The second, on 29 May, was most damaging in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramla">Ramla</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>; contemporary sources often merge the two.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-peninsula">Arabian Peninsula</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1229">1229 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">797 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Frederick II crowns himself King of Jerusalem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Having regained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> by treaty while excommunicated, the Emperor took the crown from the altar of the Holy Sepulchre and placed it on his own head. No cleric would crown him.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1241">1241 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">785 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongols defeat the Polish armies at the Battle of Chmielnik</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the first Mongol invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, Mongol forces defeated the Polish armies of Sandomierz and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a> near Chmielnik, between Kraków and Kielce. The invasion culminated in the Mongol victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legnica">Legnica</a> in April.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-mongol-invasion-of-poland">First Mongol invasion of Poland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1848">1848 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Street fighting erupts in Berlin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Troops fired on a crowd outside the royal palace and barricade fighting spread through the city, leaving hundreds dead. King Frederick William IV withdrew the army and promised a constitution.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1871">1871 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">155 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Parisians rise up and begin the Paris Commune</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Attempts by the government to remove the National Guard's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montmartre">Montmartre</a> provoked an uprising. The Commune ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> until it was crushed in the 'Bloody Week' of May.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1965">1965 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexei Leonov makes the first spacewalk</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet cosmonaut spent about 12 minutes outside Voskhod 2. His suit ballooned in the vacuum, and he had to let out air to squeeze back into the airlock.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1990">1990 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">36 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">East Germany holds its first free elections</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">East Germans voted in their first free parliamentary elections. The conservative Alliance for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> won, opening the way to rapid reunification with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a> in October.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2014">2014 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">12 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Russia signs a treaty annexing Crimea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two days after a referendum held under Russian military control, Vladimir Putin signed a treaty absorbing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>. Most UN members regard the annexation as illegal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 18 March <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-of-denmark"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-iii-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick III of Denmark</span><span class="tp">1609–1670</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/grover-cleveland"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/grover-cleveland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Grover Cleveland</span><span class="tp">1837–1908</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-diesel"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rudolf-diesel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rudolf Diesel</span><span class="tp">1858–1913</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/galeazzo-ciano"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/galeazzo-ciano.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Galeazzo Ciano</span><span class="tp">1903–1944</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/f-w-de-klerk"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/f-w-de-klerk.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">F. W. de Klerk</span><span class="tp">1936–2021</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 18 March <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-honorius-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Honorius III</span><span class="tp">1150–1227</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/matthew-iii-csak"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/matthew-iii-csak.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Matthew III Csák</span><span class="tp">c. 1260–1321</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-walpole"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-walpole.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert Walpole</span><span class="tp">1676–1745</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-i-of-greece"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-i-of-greece.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George I of Greece</span><span class="tp">1845–1913</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/eleftherios-venizelos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eleftherios-venizelos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Eleftherios Venizelos</span><span class="tp">1864–1936</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/farouk-of-egypt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/farouk-of-egypt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Farouk of Egypt</span><span class="tp">1920–1965</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/umberto-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/umberto-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Umberto II</span><span class="tp">1904–1983</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
